&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build system tests that prove Graphcore’s software works across the full stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a System Software Engineer in Test, you will develop integration and system tests across firmware and device drivers. Your work will help validate the software foundations behind Graphcore’s next-generation products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, automate and report tests for complex system features. You will also manage hardware resources, develop packaging solutions and improve CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role gives you direct exposure to low level software, hardware and cross-team integration. You will learn quickly, solve practical problems and help raise release confidence across the system software stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the integration and system test team within System Software QA. The team verifies integrated components across BMC, firmware and Linux device drivers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work happens through close partnership with developers and QA engineers. You will turn real use cases into integration and acceptance tests that protect product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decisions are made through technical discussion, review and clear evidence. You will take responsibility for your work, speak up early and move important tests forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience in low level system testing and integration solutions.&lt;br&gt;· Test development capability using C/C++ and Python.&lt;br&gt;· Experience with CI/CD, build tools and modern testing practices.&lt;br&gt;· Ability to develop integration and acceptance tests from real use cases.&lt;br&gt;· Strong communication skills, with the ability to document technical work clearly.&lt;br&gt;· Curiosity to work close to hardware, firmware, drivers and complex system behaviour.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. If you meet most of our essential criteria, we encourage you to submit an application and showcase how your background makes you a strong candidate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to build the system tests that help Graphcore release trusted software? Apply now to join the team.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;135&quot; data-end=&quot;148&quot;&gt;About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;238&quot;&gt;Shape the SoC architecture behind Graphcore’s next generation AI acceleration platforms.&amp;nbsp;Graphcore is building AI compute systems that push far beyond a single chip. As a SoC Architect, you will define, specify and integrate critical subsystems for complex silicon devices.&amp;nbsp;You will work across processor, SoC and system architecture to turn product requirements into practical design choices. Your work will influence performance, integration, modelling, validation and bring-up.&amp;nbsp;This role is for someone who enjoys deep technical ownership and broad system context. You will help Graphcore deliver multiple AI silicon projects in parallel, at real scale.&amp;nbsp;You will work on interfaces, interconnects and SoC subsystems that sit at the centre of advanced AI platforms. The problems are complex, visible and difficult to find elsewhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;990&quot; data-end=&quot;1010&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;990&quot; data-end=&quot;1010&quot;&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1012&quot; data-end=&quot;1196&quot;&gt;The Silicon Architecture team sits at the point where product ambition becomes silicon reality. Architects work closely with design, verification, hardware, software and systems teams.&amp;nbsp;The team is growing because the scope is expanding. You will own meaningful technical areas, move quickly on decisions and keep momentum across groups.&amp;nbsp;Ideas are tested through modelling, specification, discussion and evidence. People are expected to speak up, take responsibility and help others move faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1510&quot; data-end=&quot;1532&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;1510&quot; data-end=&quot;1532&quot;&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1534&quot; data-end=&quot;2021&quot;&gt;· Strong understanding of computer architecture, SoC architecture or complex silicon systems&lt;br&gt;· Experience writing clear technical specifications for engineering teams&lt;br&gt;· Knowledge of RTL development, verification processes or logical design&lt;br&gt;· Ability to work across architecture, design, verification, hardware and software teams&lt;br&gt;· Domain knowledge in areas such as PCIe, DDR, LPDDR, Ethernet or on-chip networks&lt;br&gt;· Motivation to take ownership, mentor others and drive practical decisions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2023&quot; data-end=&quot;2927&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
