&lt;h2&gt;About the job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help bring the next generation of AI hardware from design into high volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll lead the industrialisation of advanced thermal cooling solutions for AI compute processors and accelerator systems. Your work will ensure designs can be built reliably, validated efficiently, and scaled for production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll shape manufacturing processes for cold plates, thermal interface materials, and mechanical assemblies. You&#39;ll work closely with design teams, manufacturing partners, and specialist suppliers to solve complex engineering challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This role offers broad technical ownership and the opportunity to influence products from development through to manufacturing deployment across a global supply chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll join the Manufacturing Technology team within Manufacturing Operations. The team works across Bristol, Cambridge, India, Taiwan, and the US to develop robust manufacturing processes for advanced hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Day to day, you&#39;ll work closely with engineering, operations, quality teams, and manufacturing partners. Decisions are driven by technical evidence, testing, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll take ownership of manufacturing readiness, solve issues during build cycles, and help improve quality, yield, and production capability.&lt;/p&gt;
